  para o peso médio de todos os homens adultos dessa população.

  \begin{enumerate}
  \def\labelenumii{(\alph{enumii})}
  \item
    \([87.750, 90.350]\)
  \item
    \([82.268, 95.832]\)
  \item
    \([87.694, 90.406]\)
  \item
    \([82.549, 95.551]\)
  \item
    \([87.910, 90.190]\)
  \end{enumerate}

  \textbf{Solution}\\
  Note, por exemplo, que \(n=25, \overline{x}=89.05, \sigma= 19.82\) e
  \(1-\alpha=0.9\), o que implica que
  \(z_{1-{\alpha\over 2}}=z_{0.95}=1.64\). Portanto, \[\begin{aligned}
  IC(\mu; 0.9\%)
  &=
  \left(89.05-{19.82 \over \sqrt{25}}\times 1.64; \, 89.05+{19.82 \over \sqrt{25}}\times 1.64\right)
  \\
  &=\left\text{$[82.549, 95.551]$}\right.
  \end{aligned}\]

